# Playwright Conventions

## 1. Locators

Role and label first: `getByRole`, then `getByLabel` or `getByPlaceholder`, then `getByText`, then `getByTestId` only when nothing higher works (say why). Never CSS or XPath. Several matches use `.filter({ hasText })`, not `.first()`.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — pages/ProgramsPage.ts
this.newProgramButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: '+ New Program' });
this.programRow = page.getByRole('row').filter({ hasText: programName });

// ❌ Bad
page.locator('.btn-primary').click();
page.getByText('Save').first().click();
```

Why: a CSS class or `.first()` follows DOM order, so a restyle or a second match clicks the wrong control.

## 2. Waiting

Wait with a web-first assertion that retries: `expect(locator).toBeVisible()`, `.toBeEnabled()`, or `.toHaveText()`. Never `waitForTimeout`, and never `expect(await locator.isVisible()).toBe(true)`.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts
await expect(modal.dialog).toBeVisible();

// ❌ Bad
await page.waitForTimeout(2000);
expect(await modal.dialog.isVisible()).toBe(true);
```

Why: a fixed sleep and a one-shot boolean pass or fail on that instant, so a slow paint becomes a flake.

## 3. Page Objects

One class per page or component. Locators are readonly constructor fields. Methods perform actions and do not assert. Specs instantiate `new XxxPage(page)`.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — pages/ProgramsPage.ts
export class ProgramsPage {
  readonly newProgramButton: Locator;
  readonly modal: NewProgramModal;
  constructor(private readonly page: Page) {
    this.newProgramButton = page.getByRole('button', { name: '+ New Program' });
    this.modal = new NewProgramModal(page);
  }
  async goto() { await this.page.goto('/programs'); }
}

// ❌ Bad — assertion and selector inside the spec, or an expect inside the POM
await expect(page.locator('#save')).toBeVisible();
async submit() { await expect(this.dialog).toBeHidden(); }
```

Why: a selector copied into every spec, or an expect hidden in the page object, breaks in one place and hides which behavior failed.

## 4. Auth

Feature specs use the stored session from the `setup` project (`playwright/.auth/user.json`). Login-page tests start with an empty `storageState` and sign in through the UI. API login is for bulk setup, a one-off script, or a stale session.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — login-page test; other specs inherit the setup project's storageState
test.use({ storageState: { cookies: [], origins: [] } });

// ❌ Bad — UI login at the start of a programs test
test('creates a program', async ({ page }) => {
  await new LoginPage(page).login();
});
```

Advised (no API-login call in the repo yet): `POST /api/auth` with `DIDAXIS_EMAIL` and `DIDAXIS_PASSWORD`, then `context.addCookies` or `setExtraHTTPHeaders` for the token. The repo refreshes with `page.request.post('/api/auth/refresh')` inside `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts`.

Why: logging in through the UI on every test adds a second flow that fails when the form is slow, and it is not the behavior under test.

## 5. Test data

| Kind | Where | Use |
|------|--------|-----|
| Happy-path values | `test-data/factories/` | Faker (or similar) with a unique suffix per call |
| Invalid / boundary sets | `test-data/invalid/*.ts` | Curated static literals (empty, whitespace, max length) |
| Secrets and base URLs | `process.env` | `DIDAXIS_URL`, `DIDAXIS_EMAIL`, `DIDAXIS_PASSWORD` only |
| Repeated routes / copy | `test-data/enums/` or shared enums | API paths, roles, UI strings used in multiple specs |

Import `test` from `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts` and call `trackProgram(uuid)` only after a real `POST /api/programs` returns **201** (`data.id`). The fixture deletes those ids. A `page.route` fulfillment is not a created program.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — factory + trackProgram after POST 201
import { expect, test } from '../fixtures/cleanup.fixture';
import { buildProgramDraft } from '../test-data/factories/program.factory';
import { INVALID_PROGRAM_NAMES } from '../test-data/invalid/program-names';

const { name, description } = buildProgramDraft();
await programsPage.createProgram(name, description, trackProgram);
await modal.fill(INVALID_PROGRAM_NAMES.whitespaceOnly, description);

// ❌ Bad
const programName = 'Web Development 2026';
test.afterAll(async () => { await page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Delete' }).click(); });
```

Example factory (`test-data/factories/program.factory.ts`):

```typescript
import { faker } from '@faker-js/faker';

export function buildProgramDraft(overrides: Partial<{ name: string; description: string }> = {}) {
  const suffix = faker.string.alphanumeric(8);
  return {
    name: overrides.name ?? `${faker.commerce.productName()} ${suffix}`,
    description: overrides.description ?? faker.lorem.paragraph(),
  };
}
```

Why: a shared name collides when tests run together, and a UI delete or an `afterAll` leaves the row behind when the test fails first.

## 6. API testing

Setup and teardown use Playwright's `request` (`page.request` in `fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts`): `DELETE /api/programs/<uuid>` with a Bearer token resolved in memory. Do not hardcode the token. Do not delete data the test did not create.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — fixtures/cleanup.fixture.ts
await page.request.delete(`${baseUrl}/api/programs/${uuid}`, {
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` },
});

// ❌ Bad
await page.request.delete(`${baseUrl}/api/programs/${uuid}`, {
  headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer eyJhbGciOi...' },
});
```

Advised (no contract check in the repo yet):

```typescript
const response = await request.post('/api/programs', { data: { name, description } });
expect(response.status()).toBe(201);
expect((await response.json()).data.id).toEqual(expect.any(String));
```

Why: a hardcoded token expires and the run deletes nothing, and a UI-only check never catches a 201 body that dropped `data.id`.

## 7. Network mocking

`page.route` fulfills only the programs response whose UI reaction is the subject: **500** / **503**, empty `{ "data": [] }`, or a malformed body. `route.continue()` every other method. Read the live error or empty-state copy before asserting. Never mock `/api/auth/*` or the call the test is verifying.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — .cursor/rules/programs-network-edge-cases.mdc
await page.route(/\/api\/programs$/, async (route) => {
  if (route.request().method() !== 'POST') {
    await route.continue();
    return;
  }
  await route.fulfill({ status: 503, contentType: 'application/json', body: '{"message":"Service Unavailable"}' });
});

// ❌ Bad
await page.route('**/*', (route) => route.fulfill({ status: 500, body: 'nope' }));
await expect(page.getByText('Something went wrong')).toBeVisible(); // string invented, not read from the app
```

Advised (no hung-request example in the repo yet): `await route.abort('timedout')` for a timeout. The repo fulfills status **408**, not an abort.

Why: a blanket fulfill hides the real API, and an invented error string fails when the app shows different copy or nothing.

## 8. Accessibility

On the programs page, two tests: an axe scan with `wcag2a` and `wcag2aa` inside `runA11yCheck`, and a keyboard path that Tabs to `programsPage.newProgramButton`, asserts `toBeFocused()`, presses Enter, and asserts `programsPage.modal.dialog` is visible. Report violations. They must not turn CI red.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — .cursor/skills/a11y-checks/SKILL.md
const results = await new AxeBuilder({ page }).withTags(['wcag2a', 'wcag2aa']).analyze();
await expect(results.violations).toEqual([]);
await expect(programsPage.newProgramButton).toBeFocused();

// ❌ Bad
await programsPage.newProgramButton.focus();
await new AxeBuilder({ page }).disableRules(['color-contrast']).analyze();
```

Why: `.focus()` skips tab order, and `.disableRules()` hides a contrast bug the scan was there to catch.

## 9. Assertions

Assertions are web-first and live in the spec. A locator or wait change must not change what is asserted.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — tests/ds1-create-program.spec.ts
await expect(programsPage.firstProgramRow(programName)).toBeVisible();

// ❌ Bad
expect(await programsPage.firstProgramRow(programName).isVisible()).toBe(true);
```

Advised (neither is in the repo yet). Soft, when several checks belong to one test:

```typescript
await expect.soft(modal.programNameInput).toBeVisible();
await expect.soft(modal.descriptionInput).toBeVisible();
```

Visual, only when a pixel diff is the assertion that would catch the bug:

```typescript
await expect(page).toHaveScreenshot('programs-empty.png');
```

Why: a one-shot boolean stops at the first miss and does not retry; a screenshot on every screen fails on font and timezone noise.

## 10. Anti-flake

CI retries twice and local runs do not (`retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0`, never above 2). Do not set `workers: 1`. Each test uses its own data and cleans it up. Freeze relative timestamps with `page.clock.install()` before navigation. Pin `locale: 'en-CA'` and `timezoneId: 'America/Toronto'`.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — retries and trace are in playwright.config.ts; locale and timezoneId are the required pin
retries: process.env.CI ? 2 : 0,
use: { locale: 'en-CA', timezoneId: 'America/Toronto', trace: 'on-first-retry' },

// ❌ Bad
retries: 5,
workers: 1,
await page.waitForTimeout(3000);
```

Advised (no spec calls `page.clock` yet):

```typescript
await page.clock.install({ time: new Date('2026-06-15T15:00:00Z') });
await programsPage.goto();
await expect(programsPage.programRow('Web Development').getByText('2 hours ago')).toBeVisible();
```

Why: extra retries hide a real bug, `workers: 1` only slows the suite, and a live clock makes "2 hours ago" depend on when CI ran.

## 11. Tags

Each `test(...)` carries **exactly one** Playwright tag (a single string in `{ tag: '…' }`, not on `describe`). Allowed values:

| Tag | When to use |
|-----|-------------|
| `@smoke` | Fast critical path after deploy |
| `@sanity` | Core happy paths for a feature area |
| `@regression` | Broader coverage, edge cases, a11y informational checks |
| `@api` | Primary assertion is HTTP contract / `request` / cleanup fixture behavior |
| `@e2e` | Multi-step UI journey through real navigation |
| `@destructive` | Mutates **shared or global** state (locale, roles, feature flags, tenant settings) — not data this test creates and deletes via `trackProgram` |

Tests that only create records they clean up keep `@smoke`, `@sanity`, `@regression`, `@api`, or `@e2e` — not `@destructive`.

Run slices: `npm run test:smoke`, `test:sanity`, `test:regression`, `test:api`, `test:e2e`, or `test:destructive` (last sets `--workers=1`). Filter a single file with `-g` on the title when needed.

**State-mutating tests** (anything that changes shared/global state, including every `@destructive` test) must register an `test.afterEach` or `test.afterAll` hook that reverts or restores the prior state (role, locale, flag, setting). Document what was changed and how it is restored.

```typescript
// ✅ Good — one suite tag; self-cleaned program data stays @regression
test('TC-001 — form shows required fields', { tag: '@smoke' }, async ({ page, trackProgram }) => {
  const { name, description } = buildProgramDraft();
  await programsPage.createProgram(name, description, trackProgram);
});

// ✅ Good — @destructive + explicit revert
test('switches tenant locale to fr-CA', { tag: '@destructive' }, async ({ page }) => {
  const previousLocale = await readTenantLocale(page);
  try {
    await setTenantLocale(page, 'fr-CA');
    // … assertions …
  } finally {
    await setTenantLocale(page, previousLocale);
  }
});
test.afterEach(async ({ page }) => {
  await setTenantLocale(page, 'en-CA'); // or read from env default
});

// ❌ Bad — two tags, or @destructive for trackProgram-only data
test('creates program', { tag: ['@smoke', '@e2e'] }, async () => {});
test.describe('@regression', () => { /* … */ });
```

Why: one tag keeps `npm run test:*` predictable; `@destructive` serializes only what can poison other workers; revert hooks stop flaky shared state from leaking across specs.

## Do / Don't

| | Do | Don't |
|---|---|---|
| 1 Locators | `getByRole` → label / placeholder → text → `getByTestId` (say why); `.filter({ hasText })` | CSS, XPath, `.first()` |
| 2 Waiting | `expect(locator).toBeVisible()` / `.toBeEnabled()` / `.toHaveText()` | `waitForTimeout`, `expect(await locator.isVisible()).toBe(true)` |
| 3 Page Objects | One class per page or component; locators in the constructor; actions only | `expect` inside `pages/`, selectors repeated in the spec |
| 4 Auth | `storageState` from the setup project; empty storage only for the login page | `login()` in a feature spec |
| 5 Test data | Factories under `test-data/factories/`; invalid sets in `test-data/invalid/`; `trackProgram` after POST **201** | A fixed name, UI delete, or `afterAll` |
| 6 API testing | `page.request` delete of ids this test created | A hardcoded Bearer token |
| 7 Network mocking | Fulfill one programs response (500/503, empty, malformed); assert live copy | `page.route('**/*')`, invented error text, mocking `/api/auth/*` |
| 8 Accessibility | Axe `wcag2a` + `wcag2aa`; Tab to the control, then Enter | `.focus()`, `.disableRules()` to force green |
| 9 Assertions | Web-first `expect` in the spec | A snapshot boolean; a screenshot that is not the point of the test |
| 10 Anti-flake | CI retries 2, local 0; `en-CA` / `America/Toronto`; `page.clock` for relative time | `retries` above 2, `workers: 1`, the wall clock |
| 11 Tags | Exactly one of `@smoke` … `@destructive` on each `test()`; revert hook on shared-state changes | Tags on `describe`, multiple tags, `@destructive` for self-cleaned data |

## Refusals (hard stops)

Stop and raise the conflict — do not comply, weaken, or work around:

- Never weaken or delete an assertion to make a test pass.
- Never heal a failure triage classified as a real app bug.
- Never replace a role-based locator with CSS or XPath.
- Never use `waitForTimeout`.
- Never hardcode a credential.
- Never use the `any` type.
